A||N||3||Haze_Performance||Looking for header info..||||14||
Z||000000||Haze_Performance||05-03-2001||07:07 PM||||Well I know the header posts have been beaten to death but...<P>I'm looking for a nice set of affordable headers for a '88 Formula. The Fiero Store sells the sprint manifolds for over $500!!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"><P>Anyone know where I can pick-up headers for well under that price? <P>TIA  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><BR><I>Haze</I><P>------------------<BR><A HREF="http://www.ws6fiero.com" TARGET=_blank><BR>         <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/haze8588logo.gif">    </A>       <BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/WS6_Fiero/photo.html" TARGET=_blank><BR>Pennock's Fiero Forum Members Photo Page</A><P><A HREF="http://www.clubs.yahoo.com/clubs/ws6fiero" TARGET=_blank>WS6 Fiero Club</A>||||reg||14
Z||000001||Dave Gunsul||05-03-2001||07:38 PM||||We get a 10% discount from the Fiero store<BR>so they're only $495.00. ;-)<BR>The only way you're going to get lower priced headers is to find someone who's selling a used set or you can get a set of manifolds ported from Darrell Morse.<BR>Darrell only charges $150.00 for the porting.<BR>If you do this though I would recomend that you take the ported manifolds in and have them Jet Hot coated too. I know of a place in Yorkville that does this, probably cost 100-150 for the coating. <P>------------------<BR>Dave Gunsul<BR>N.I.F.E. member<BR>86 GT modified<BR>85 SE daily driver||||reg||1
Z||000002||WKDFIRO||05-03-2001||07:47 PM||||I guess the answer would be no.<P>There are no headers out there for the Fiero V6 well under $500....unless you go ported manifolds which actually are good for some performance for what you pay.||||reg||9
Z||000003||Oreif||05-03-2001||08:35 PM||||Chris West sells a set of "Shorty" headers. They are very simular to the Sprints but they only cost $395.00 for the set.<BR>see link:<BR> <A HREF="http://www.cwestco.com/Exhaust/Exhaust.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.cwestco.com/Exhaust/Exhaust.html</A> <P>I think they will bolt up to the stock "Y" pipe but am not sure.<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg"> ||||reg||4
